\ User-declarable trait bounds (P7.S3e). A trait lists required member
\ signatures, one type variable per trait; `impl:` binds a type's concrete
\ words to those members. A poly word can then require a bound (`'T: Order`)
\ instead of hardcoding one type, and each required member dispatches to the
\ caller's own `impl:` at monomorphization -- an ordinary word call resolved
\ per instantiation, never a runtime vtable.

import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude | if lt gt | ;
import: core::bool | Bool | ;

type: Ordering
| Less
| Equal
| Greater
;

trait: Order 'T
  cmp ( &'T &'T -- Ordering )
;

trait: Show 'T
  show ( &'T -- )
;

type: Point x i64 y i64 ;

\ Satisfaction is nominal, not structural: an explicit `impl:` block binds a
\ type's own concrete words to a trait's members. A member's signature must
\ match the trait's exactly, with the trait's `'T` substituted for the
\ concrete type.
: point-cmp ( &Point &Point -- Ordering )
  | a b |
  a &y @ | ay | 
  b &y @ | by |
  ay by lt
  ~[ Less ]
  ~[
    ay by gt 
    ~[ Greater ]
    ~[
      a &x @ | ax |
      b &x @ | bx |
      ax bx lt
      ~[ Less ]
      ~[
        ax bx gt 
        ~[ Greater ] ~[ Equal ] if
      ] if
    ] if
  ] if ;

: point-show ( &Point -- )
  | p | "(" . p &x @ . "," . p &y @ . ")" . ;

impl: Order for Point  cmp point-cmp ;
impl: Show for Point  show point-show ;

\ Bounds compose: `'T: Order Show` is the existing `'T: Copy Ord`-style
\ capability list, greedy over N names. `cmp`/`show` dispatch as ordinary
\ required members, resolved against the caller's own `impl:` at
\ monomorphization -- an ordinary word call, never a quotation value or a
\ runtime vtable.
: show_larger ( &'T: Order Show &'T -- )
  | b | | a |
  a b cmp
  ~[ ( Less ) drop b show ]
  ~[ ( Equal ) drop a show ]
  ~[ ( Greater ) drop a show ]
  Ordering? ;

: main ( -- )
  0 0 Point | origin |
  3 4 Point | corner |
  &origin &corner show_larger
  origin drop
  corner drop ;
